  "notes": "<ul>\n<li><ol start=\"1137\">\n<li>N-th Tribonacci Number</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li></li>\n<li>Difficulty: easy</li>\n<li>Tags: math, dynamic-programming, memoization</li>\n<li></li>\n<li>Description:</li>\n<li>The Tribonacci sequence T_n is defined as follows:</li>\n<li></li>\n<li>T_0 = 0, T_1 = 1, T_2 = 1, and T_n+3 = T_n + T_n+1 + T_n+2 for n &gt;= 0.</li>\n<li></li>\n<li>Given <code>n</code>, return the value of T_n.</li>\n<li></li>\n<li>Examples:</li>\n<li><ol>\n<li>Input: n = 4</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li>Output: 4</li>\n<li>Explanation: T_3 = 0 + 1 + 1 = 2 T_4 = 1 + 1 + 2 = 4</li>\n<li><ol start=\"2\">\n<li>Input: n = 25</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li>Output: 1389537</li>\n<li></li>\n<li>Constraints:</li>\n<li><ul>\n<li><code>0 &lt;= n &lt;= 37</code></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><ul>\n<li>The answer is guaranteed to fit within a 32-bit integer, ie. <code>answer &lt;= 2^31 - 1</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li></li>\n</ul>\n",
